For clarity, the above Law provides, among other things, that:

• Article 9 — copyright arises by virtue of the fact of creation of a work;
  registration or other formalities are not required for copyright to arise;
• Article 15 — the author has personal non-property rights, including the right
  to be recognized as the author; such rights are retained independently of
  economic rights and are non-transferable; and
• Article 16 — the author or other right holder possesses exclusive economic
  rights to use the work in any form and by any method, subject to limitations
